end{bmatrix}.$ Find $3a+2b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186120307 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b41bd59f-46c7-542b-bca0-d17f42387db0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120307 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply each component of $a$ by $3$ and each component of $b$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9-6 \\\\ 6-4 \\\\ 15+2 \\\\ 3+10 \\\\ -6+12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1071 "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$, then $u\\cdot v=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b6cc7d3-d9ee-56cd-98e9-b1d240810c8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120308 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 6+3\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-8-4+12-21 \\\\  & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120373 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186118352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120373 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35131" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120373 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$. What is $(2u) \\cdot v$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120373 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "391a69b1-ee1e-5f21-86b9-768ef1e52739" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120666 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120666 #edb/ref 1061 17446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120666 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7383fe70-62a2-5560-94ff-c67e603fd1a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120666 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120667 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120667 #edb/ref 1061 17447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120667 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5cfee280-6899-59d1-9ef8-d9880087735a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120667 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120668 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120668 #edb/ref 1061 17448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120668 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5aec48fe-0c24-5fa5-ac63-78e2260f7ead" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120668 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120669 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120669 #edb/ref 1061 17449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120669 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "21085223-43d0-5726-b75d-b102bd093330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120669 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120670 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120670 #edb/ref 1061 17450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120670 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4acc22bf-58df-50bc-b180-3077f975037c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120670 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120671 #edb/ref 1061 17451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120671 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "36416450-4cfa-51cd-be65-4dead60ba52e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120671 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120747 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120747 #edb/ref 1061 23156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120747 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6574b7ab-c36d-5af6-9074-943a1db9174c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120747 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121032 #edb/ref 1064 "The **real coordinate space** (of dimension $n$) is the set of all possible column vectors of height $n,$ whose components are real numbers. Symbolically, we represent the real coordinate space of dimension $n$ as $\\mathbb{R}^n.$\n\nFor example, the following vectors are in $\\mathbb{R}, \\mathbb{R}^2,$ $\\mathbb{R}^3,$ and $\\mathbb{R}^5,$ respectively: \n\n![](images/20/20e0adb04d7a8711cad4a9ee7ad26755d52176fc9549d7809fe10665a8118945.svg)\n\nWe've already encountered several operations on vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ or $\\mathbb{R}^3,$ namely, vector addition and subtraction, scalar multiplication, and the dot product. All of these operations work the same way in $\\mathbb{R}^n.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121032 #edb/ref 1065 3182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121032 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "084d7eb8-e6bd-5678-98b5-149f18e61a8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121032 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121033 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, if we have two vectors $\\mathbf{u},\\mathbf{v}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ and a scalar $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb{R},$ then our vector operations are defined as follows:\n\n- The **sum/difference** of the two vectors is defined as\n![](images/fc/fc78b2f4e9262108a217e57fec67e096b8b8b18e1486bec8e51df60b8afdfdfa.svg)\n\n- **Scalar multiplication** of a vector is defined as\n![](images/e7/e78025f3481423365b2e924b6f8ba4e59f41e0c644ced7d2263238b219cba27a.svg)\n\n- The **dot product** of two vectors is defined as\n\n$$\n\\quad \\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v} = \\underbrace{u_1 \\cdot v_1 + u_2 \\cdot v_2 + \\cdots + u_n \\cdot v_n}_{\\Large{n} \\,\\textrm{-terms}} = \\sum_{i=1}^n u_i v_i.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121033 #edb/ref 1065 3183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121033 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a465d6d9-270d-5cd3-98c8-a78c527b3558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121033 #edb/ref 1067 "General Rules" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121062 #edb/ref 1064 "To add two vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^n,$ we just need to add their corresponding components. To illustrate, consider the vectors $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b} \\in \\mathbb{R}^4,$ given by\n\n![](images/1f/1f1b79f2e61fccbb27944284cbdd217a311a7f795100cfbb56340a457814b407.svg)\n\nTo compute $\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b},$ all we have to do is to add each component of the vector $\\mathbf{a}$ with the corresponding component of $\\mathbf{b}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5+(-5) \\\\ 1+3 \\\\ -3+1 \\\\ 6+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can only compute the sum, difference, or dot product of two vectors if both vectors have the same number of components. For example, we can't find the following sum, so we say it's *undefined*:\n![](images/6c/6c377966aa9fa1d581c0f9e3ba16bceb4020471914d5c4fb61118ff7cd709466.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186121062 #edb/ref 1065 3922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121062 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "34cc8b84-ed7a-54e2-995c-12a2b57b0ff0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121062 #edb/ref 1067 "Adding Two Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315124 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186315124 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315124 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "016d9ebc-610a-5f44-9c37-f3eb046a7735" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315470 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 